\n\
Actually, let me think — I should play the Island first (in case of something weird), then cast Sokka. Order matters little here, but playing Island first is good since it enters untapped and could pay for things. Actually, wait — if I play Island, I have 4 untapped lands + Waterskin = 5 mana. But Sokka costs 4, so I don't need it. Still, playing the land is free value.\n\
\n\
Which land to play? Island gives me more blue. I already have Plains and Mountain and Gates. Let me play Island — it enters untapped, giving me the most flexibility.\n\
\n\
Then cast Sokka with the remaining mana. Sokka is a 3/3 menace prowess that makes Allies have menace/prowess and creates tokens on noncreature spells. Great against their board — menace means they need 2 blockers.\n\
