      "reasoning": "Opponent is swinging with Pakku again, but they're completely tapped out — no tricks possible. Sokka (3/3) blocks Pakku (2/4), both survive, and I take zero damage. Free block.",
      "thinking": "Opponent attacked with Master Pakku (2/4). I have Sokka 3/3 with menace. Blocking: Sokka 3/3 vs Pakku 2/4 — Sokka deals 3 to Pakku (2 toughness... wait Pakku is 2/4, so 3 damage doesn't kill it), Pakku deals 2 to Sokka (3 toughness), Sokka survives. Trade isn't great — Pakku survives at 2/4 with 3 damage... actually damage clears at end of turn. Sokka takes 2, survives. Pakku takes 3, survives (4 toughness). So nothing dies, but I prevent 2 damage.\n\
\n\
Should I block? Sokka is my key engine. Risk: opponent could have a pump spell... they're tapped out (all lands tapped). Actually they attacked with just Pakku, mana all tapped — they can't pump. Blocking means Sokka survives (2 damage to a 3/3). I take 0 instead of 2.\n\
\n\
But wait — do I want to block with my engine? Sokka survives for sure since opponent is tapped out (no tricks). All four of their lands are tapped. So blocking is safe: Sokka takes 2, lives, Pakku lives. I save 2 life.\n\
\n\
Actually, is there a reason not to block? If Sokka is tapped... no, blocking doesn't tap Sokka unless... blocking doesn't tap. Sokka stays untapped. Fine.\n\
\n\
Hmm, but wait — War Balloon is on their side. They might crew it next turn. That's their plan (\"take to the air\").\n\
\n\
I'll block with Sokka. Actually, let me think — is 2 life worth the risk? They're fully tapped, no tricks possible. Sokka at 3/3 blocks 2/4, survives. Yes, block.\n\
\n\
Actually wait, one consideration: prowess — Pakku gets +1/+1 when they cast noncreature spells, but they can't cast now (tapped out). Safe.\n\
\n\
Block with Sokka.",
