      "thinking": "I'm at turn 6, precombat main. I planned to play an untapped Plains, then cast Rowdy Snowballers to stun Katara and attack.\n\
\n\
Let me look at the board:\n\
\n\
My board:\n\
- Ally Token (1/1, menace, prowess)\n\
- Bender's Waterskin\n\
- Island x2, Mountain, North Pole Gates, Plains x2\n\
- Sokka (3/3, menace, prowess)\n\
\n\
My hand: North Pole Gates (land), Plains (land), Rowdy Snowballers (2U), Sun-Blessed Peak (land)\n\
\n\
Opponent's board:\n\
- Airship Engine Room x3 (tapped)\n\
- Island x2 (tapped)\n\
- Jeong Jeong (2/3, tapped, summoning sick)\n\
- Katara (3/4 with +1/+1 counter, tapped)\n\
- Master Pakku (1/3, tapped)\n\
- War Balloon (untapped, not a creature — 0 fire counters, needs crew 3)\n\
\n\
Opponent at 16 life, tapped out. Opponent has 2 cards in hand.\n\
\n\
Plan: Play Plains (untapped), cast Rowdy Snowballers (2U) targeting Katara — stun counter keeps her tapped through their next untap. Rowdy Snowballers is a creature spell — wait, does it trigger Sokka's prowess? No! Prowess triggers on noncreature spells. Rowdy Snowballers is a creature, so no prowess trigger, no token.\n\
\n\
Hmm, so casting Rowdy Snowballers doesn't trigger Sokka. But it stuns Katara — stun counter means when it would untap, instead remove a stun counter. So Katara stays tapped.\n\
\n\
Attack considerations: Opponent's untapped blockers next turn: after my turn, opponent untaps. Katara has stun counter — won't untap. Pakku will untap, Jeong Jeong will untap (no longer summoning sick), War Balloon can crew 3.\n\
\n\
