So Jeong Jeong's exhaust could copy a Lesson spell. That requires 3 mana + lesson cost. Possible but mana-intensive.\n\
\n\
Katara waterbend {6}: draw a card — needs 6 mana; they have 5 lands. Next turn they play a 6th land and could waterbend. But she needs to be untapped to... no wait, waterbend {6} — is it an activated ability requiring tap? \"Waterbend {6}: Draw a card.\" Hmm, waterbend abilities in this set — some require tapping. The text shown is \"Waterbend {6}: Draw a card.\" I don't know if it includes {T}. Waterbend typically is an activated ability with a cost that may include tapping. The oracle text here doesn't show a tap symbol explicitly. Let me not overthink.\n\
\n\
Decision: stun Katara. She's the biggest and her staying tapped delays their card draw engine.\n\
\n\
Hmm, but one more consideration: the stun counter keeps her tapped → she grows at end step. A 4/5 (then 5/6...) Katara is a real problem long-term. But I plan to win before that matters. My clock: 4 damage this turn (16→12), next turn more.\n\
\n\
Actually, let me think about the race more carefully. Opponent at 16. My attackers this turn: Sokka 3/3 (menace), token 1/1 (menace). Snowballers is sick. So 4 damage if unblocked. They're all tapped — unblocked. 16→12.\n\
\n\
Their turn: they untap Pakku, Jeong Jeong (Katara stays tapped if stunned). They play land #6. They can attack with Pakku (1/3, prowess), Jeong Jeong (2/3, firebending 1). Maybe crew War Balloon (crew 3: tap creatures with total power 3+ — Pakku + Jeong Jeong = 3 power, but then those can't attack; balloon is 4/4? War Balloon flying, power/toughness not shown... it's a Vehicle, probably like 3/3 or 4/4).\n\
\n\
My life at 20. Their damage: Pakku 1 + Jeong Jeong 2 = 3 (plus prowess if they cast spells). Not scary. I can also block.\n\
\n\
My next turn: attack with Sokka, token, Snowballers (all menace). They have Pakku, Jeong Jeong, Katara (untaps... no wait, Katara stunned stays tapped through their turn, then my turn she's still tapped? Stun counter: \"If a permanent with a stun counter on it would become untapped, instead remove a stun counter from it.\" Actually the rule: during untap step, permanents with stun counters don't untap; remove a stun counter instead. Hmm, precisely: 122.1c? The stun counter rule: \"If a tapped permanent with a stun counter on it would become untapped, a stun counter is removed from it instead. This is a replacement effect.\" So during their untap step, Katara would untap → instead remove stun counter, stays tapped. She remains tapped through their turn. On their NEXT untap step, she untaps normally.\n\
\n\
So on my next turn, Katara is still tapped. Their blockers: Pakku + Jeong Jeong only. They can double-block one of my three menace attackers. I attack with Sokka 3/3, token 1/1, Snowballers 2/2 = 6 power. If they double-block Sokka: Sokka deals 3 to Jeong Jeong (kills), takes 3 (1 from Pakku + 2 from JJ) → Sokka dies. Trade Sokka for Jeong Jeong, and token + Snowballers deal 3 → 12→9. Hmm, losing Sokka is bad.\n\
\n\
Alternatively they might not block. We'll see.\n\
\n\
Anyway — stun Katara. Let me do it.\n\
\n\
Actually, wait. Should I consider stunning Jeong Jeong instead, so that... no. Katara is clearly the best stun target: biggest body, and keeping her tapped delays their waterbend card draw. The growth counter is a minor downside.\n\
\n\
One more angle: stunning Pakku prevents mill triggers? Pakku mills when it becomes tapped. If Pakku is stunned (stays tapped), it can't attack (can't become tapped by attacking), so no mill. But mill 3 isn't verythreatening. Katara remains the choice.\n\
\n\
Let me choose Katara (p34).",
