- Bender's Waterskin - untapped\n\
- Island x2, Mountain, North Pole Gates, Plains x3 - all untapped\n\
- Rowdy Snowballers (2/2, menace, prowess) - untapped\n\
- Sokka (3/3, menace, prowess) - untapped\n\
\n\
**Opponent's board (PilotB, 12 life):**\n\
- Airship Engine Room x3 - tapped\n\
- Boar-q-pine (2/2) - untapped, summoning sick\n\
- Island x2 - tapped\n\
- Jeong Jeong (2/3) - tapped\n\
- Katara (4/5 with 2 +1/+1 counters) - tapped (stunned)\n\
- Master Pakku (1/3) - untapped\n\
- Mountain - untapped\n\
- War Balloon (4/3 flyer with 3 fire counters) - untapped\n\
\n\
**My hand:** North Pole Gates, Plains, Sun-Blessed Peak (all lands)\n\
\n\
It's my turn 7, precombat main. I planned to play Plains and attack with my three menace creatures (Sokka 3/3, Rowdy Snowballers 2/2, Ally Token 1/1).\n\
\n\
Opponent's untapped blockers: Boar-q-pine (2/2), Master Pakku (1/3), War Balloon (4/3 flyer).\n\
\n\
Wait, War Balloon has 3 fire counters so it's an artifact creature now (4/3 flyer). It can block.\n\
\n\
Menace requires 2+ blockers per attacker. They have 3 untapped creatures: Boar-q-pine, Pakku, War Balloon.\n\
\n\
If I attack with all three menace creatures:\n\
- Each attacker needs 2 blockers\n\
- They have 3 blockers total, so they can fully block at most one attacker (using 2 of 3 blockers), leaving 1 blocker which can't block any menace creature alone.\n\
\n\
So at least two of my attackers get through unblocked... wait, let me think. They have 3 blockers. Each menace attacker needs 2 blockers to be blocked. With 3 blockers, they can block one attacker with 2 creatures, and the third blocker can't block anything (menace). So two attackers get through: Sokka (3) + Snowballers (2) = 5 damage, or Sokka + token = 4, or Snowballers + token = 3.\n\
\n\
They'd obviously block the biggest threat. They'd block Sokka with 2 creatures, letting Snowballers (2) and token (1) through = 3 damage. Opponent at 12 → 9.\n\
\n\
Alternatively, if they double-block Sokka: which creatures? War Balloon (4/3) + Boar-q-pine (2/2): Sokka deals 3 damage, killing Boar-q-pine and dealing 1 to War Balloon. Sokka takes 6 damage and dies. Hmm, that's bad — I'd lose Sokka.\n\
\n\
Wait, but I also need to consider: do I have any tricks? My hand is all lands. No tricks.\n\
\n\
Actually, let me reconsider. Should I attack with all three?\n\
\n\
Blockers: War Balloon 4/3, Boar-q-pine 2/2, Pakku 1/3.\n\
\n\
If they double-block Sokka (3/3) with War Balloon + Pakku: Sokka kills Pakku (1 damage) and deals 2 to War Balloon; Sokka takes 5 damage and dies. Bad.\n\
\n\
If they double-block Sokka with War Balloon + Boar-q-pine: Sokka deals... I choose damage assignment order. I'd order War Balloon first (kill the 4/3 flyer — the biggest threat). Sokka deals 3 to War Balloon (lethal), then 0 to Boar-q-pine... wait, must assign lethal to first before moving on. 3 damage to War Balloon kills it (3 toughness). Then no damage left for Boar-q-pine. Sokka takes 4+2=6 damage and dies. Hmm, trade Sokka for War Balloon. Or order Boar-q-pine first: 2 damage kills it, 1 damage to War Balloon. Sokka takes 6 and dies. Trade Sokka for Boar-q-pine + 1 damage to balloon. Bad.\n\
\n\
Hmm, so attacking with Sokka into double-block means Sokka dies. That kills my engine.\n\
\n\
But wait — would the opponent actually double-block Sokka? They know Sokka is my engine (making tokens, giving menace). They probably would trade two creatures for Sokka... Actually from their perspective: they block Sokka with War Balloon + Boar-q-pine. Sokka (3/3) kills one of them and dies to the combined 6 damage. They lose a creature + I lose Sokka, but my Snowballers (2) and token (1) get through for 3 damage → they go to 9.\n\
\n\
Alternatively they could just take the damage: no blocks, take 6 → go to 6 life.\n\
\n\
Hmm, what's my best play here? Let me think about what happens if I don't attack with Sokka, and just attack with Snowballers + token:\n\
\n\
They can block Snowballers with 2 of their 3 blockers (e.g., War Balloon + Pakku), killing it (Snowballers deals 2 to War Balloon, takes 5... wait War Balloon 4 + Pakku 1 = 5 damage to the 2/2, dead; Snowballers assigns 2 damage — kills Pakku if ordered first (1 damage... Pakku has 3 toughness, 2 damage doesn't kill). Hmm: Snowballers 2/2 blocked by War Balloon (4/3) + Pakku (1/3): Snowballers assigns 2 damage. If order Pakku first: 2 damage to Pakku (3 toughness, survives with 2 marked). War Balloon and Pakku deal 5 to Snowballers, dead. Token gets through for 1. Opponent at 11.\n\
\n\
That's weak. \n\
\n\
Alternatively, attack with all three. Opponent's best block: double-block Sokka (biggest), take 3 from Snowballers + token → 9 life. Sokka dies but takes a blocker down.\n\
\n\
Hmm wait, actually let me reconsider — is there a better option? What if I attack with only Sokka and token, keeping Snowballers back? Same problem — they double-block Sokka with their two best, Sokka dies, token gets through for 1.\n\
\n\
What if I attack with Sokka alone? They double block with War Balloon + Boar-q-pine, Sokka dies killing one. Or they take 3 → 9 life. They'd probably block and kill Sokka.\n\
\n\
Hmm. Actually, would they? Let's think from opponent's perspective at 12 life. If they double-block Sokka with War Balloon + Boar-q-pine: I assign 3 damage — I'd kill War Balloon (their best creature) for sure. They lose War Balloon + Sokka dies. Then my board: Snowballers 2/2 menace, token 1/1 menace. Their board: Boar-q-pine 2/2, Pakku 1/3, Katara 4/5 (stunned, untaps... wait Katara has a stun counter — she stays tapped through their next untap, then the stun counter is removed? No wait — stun counter: when the permanent would untap, instead remove a stun counter. Katara has a stun counter from Snowballers. So on opponent's next untap step, Katara doesn't untap and removes the stun counter. So Katara stays tapped through their next turn), Jeong Jeong tapped (untaps next turn).\n\
\n\
