      "reasoning": "War Balloon is the real threat — a 4/3 flyer that can crew itself. Pakku's mill is slow and non-lethal. Putting all 3 damage on War Balloon to kill it.",
      "thinking": "I'm assigning combat damage with Sokka (3/3) against War Balloon (4/3) and Master Pakku (1/3). I need to assign 3 damage total.\n\
\n\
War Balloon is the bigger threat — a 4/3 flyer. Pakku is a 1/3 with mill potential. If I assign 3 to War Balloon, it dies (3 toughness). Pakku survives. Sokka takes 4+1=5 damage and dies.\n\
\n\
Alternatively, kill Pakku? War Balloon is the more dangerous threat — it's a 4/3 flyer that can attack me. Pakku mills me but I'm at 24 cards in library, not an immediate concern. Pakku's mill scales with Lesson cards in their graveyard — they have Airbending Lesson... wait that's my graveyard. Their graveyard has Abandon Attachments x2, Boomerang Basics, The Cave of Two Lovers, The Legend of Roku — lessons? Airbending Lesson is a Lesson. It says \"Lesson cards in your graveyard: 3\" — so Pakku mills 3 when tapped. Not a huge threat.\n\
\n\
War Balloon as a 4/3 flyer is the real threat. Kill it. Assign 3 to War Balloon, 0 to Pakku.\n\
\n\
Wait — but ordering rules: I must assign lethal damage to the first blocker before assigning to the next. War Balloon has 3 toughness, so 3 damage kills it. That's fine.\n\
\n\
Assign [3,0].",
